  {
   "MatterHistoryAccelaRecordId": null,
   "MatterHistoryActionBodyId": 138,
   "MatterHistoryActionBodyName": "Metropolitan Council",
   "MatterHistoryActionDate": "2026-07-21T18:00:00",
   "MatterHistoryActionId": 391,
   "MatterHistoryActionName": "passed on second reading",
   "MatterHistoryActionText": "The bill was approved by the Arts, Parks, Libraries, and Entertainment Committee. Council Member Vo moved that the bill be passed on second reading, which motion was properly seconded. Council Member Styles moved that the bill be deferred, which motion was properly seconded. After discussion, Council Member Parker called for the previous question, which motion was seconded and approved by a voice vote of the Council. The matter recurred on the motion to defer the bill, which motion was seconded and failed by the following roll call vote: Yes (10): Kimbrough, Cortese, Eslick, Evans, Welsch, Cash, Druffel, Johnston, Styles, and Lee; No (25): Porterfield, Evans-Segall, Allen, Hill, Toombs, Gamble, Parker, Capp, Benedict, Harrell, Hancock, Bradford, Huffman, Vo, Horton, Taylor, Gadd, Preptit, Nash, Benton, Ellis, Sepulveda, Rutherford, Ewing, and Spain; Abstain (1): Kupin. The matter recurred on the motion that the bill be passed on second reading, which motion was properly seconded. Council Member Kupin offered a proposed amendment and moved that it be adopted, which motion was seconded and failed by a voice vote of the Council. The matter recurred on the motion that the bill be passed on second reading, which motion was properly seconded. After discussion, Council Member Benedict called for the previous question, which motion was seconded and approved by a voice vote of the Council. The matter recurred on the motion that the bill be passed on second reading, which motion was seconded and approved by the following roll call vote:",
